      "source": [
        "# Digital Design - mod-22\n\n",
        "**Course:** digital-design\n\n",
        "Run the code cells below to practice.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Example: 1024 x 8 memory (1KB)\n- 10 address lines (2^10 = 1024 locations)\n- 8 data lines (each location stores 8 bits)\n- Total capacity: 1024 x 8 = 8192 bits = 1 KB\n\nBlock Diagram:\n         Address [9:0]\n              \u2502\n              \u25bc\n    \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n    \u2502                  \u2502\n    \u2502   1024 x 8      \u2502\n    \u2502   Memory Array   \u2502\u2500\u2500\u2192 Data Out [7:0]\n    \u2502                  \u2502\n    \u2502                  \u2502\u2190\u2500\u2500 Data In [7:0]\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n         \u2191    \u2191    \u2191\n        CS   WE   OE\n  (Chip Select, Write Enable, Output Enable)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "A ROM is essentially a decoder + OR array:\n\nAddress \u2192 [Decoder] \u2192 Selects one word line\n                    \u2192 Each word line activates stored data on bit lines\n                    \u2192 Data appears on output\n\nFor a 4x4 ROM:\nAddress A1,A0 \u2192 2-to-4 decoder \u2192 selects one of 4 rows\nEach row has 4 stored bits (connected or not to bit lines)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Word Line\n              \u2502\n    \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n    \u2502         \u2502         \u2502\n   [T1]      \u2502        [T2]  (access transistors)\n    \u2502         \u2502         \u2502\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500\u2192[INV]\u2500\u253c\u2500[INV]\u2190\u2500\u2500\u2524   (cross-coupled inverters)\n    \u2502         \u2502         \u2502\n   BL        \u2502        BL'   (bit lines)\n         (complementary)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Word Line\n        \u2502\n       [T1] (access transistor)\n        \u2502\n       [C]  (storage capacitor)\n        \u2502\n       GND\n\nStores: Charged capacitor = 1, Discharged = 0"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Example: 64KB memory using 16KB chips\n\nAddress space: 0x0000 to 0xFFFF (16 address bits)\n\nChip 0: 0x0000-0x3FFF (A15=0, A14=0)\nChip 1: 0x4000-0x7FFF (A15=0, A14=1)\nChip 2: 0x8000-0xBFFF (A15=1, A14=0)\nChip 3: 0xC000-0xFFFF (A15=1, A14=1)\n\nA15,A14 \u2192 2-to-4 decoder \u2192 Chip Select signals\nA13-A0  \u2192 directly to all chips (internal addressing)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Address:  \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2571 Valid Address \u2572\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nCS:       \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2572______________\u2571\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n                     \u2502\u2190\u2500 tAA \u2500\u2192\u2502\nData Out: \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2571Valid\u2572\n                     \ntAA = Address Access Time (address stable to data valid)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Address:  \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2571 Valid Address \u2572\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nWE:       \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2572______________\u2571\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nData In:  \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2571 Valid Data \u2572\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n                   \u2502\u2190 tWD \u2192\u2502\n                   \ntWD = Write Data Setup Time"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "verilog",
          "// ROM (initialized with $readmemh or initial block)\nmodule rom_256x8(\n    input  wire [7:0] address,\n    input  wire       cs,\n    output wire [7:0] data_out\n);\n    reg [7:0] memory [0:255];\n    \n    initial begin\n        memory[0] = 8'hA5;\n        memory[1] = 8'h3C;\n        memory[2] = 8'hFF;\n        // ... more initialization\n    end\n    \n    assign data_out = cs ? memory[address] : 8'bz;\nendmodule"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "verilog",
          "// Single-port SRAM\nmodule sram_1024x8(\n    input  wire        clk,\n    input  wire        cs,\n    input  wire        we,\n    input  wire [9:0]  address,\n    input  wire [7:0]  data_in,\n    output reg  [7:0]  data_out\n);\n    reg [7:0] memory [0:1023];\n    \n    always @(posedge clk) begin\n        if (cs) begin\n            if (we)\n                memory[address] <= data_in;\n            else\n                data_out <= memory[address];\n        end\n    end\nendmodule"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "verilog",
          "// Dual-port RAM (simultaneous read and write)\nmodule dual_port_ram #(\n    parameter ADDR_WIDTH = 10,\n    parameter DATA_WIDTH = 8\n)(\n    input  wire                    clk,\n    // Port A (Read/Write)\n    input  wire                    we_a,\n    input  wire [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0]  addr_a,\n    input  wire [DATA_WIDTH-1:0]  din_a,\n    output reg  [DATA_WIDTH-1:0]  dout_a,\n    // Port B (Read only)\n    input  wire [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0]  addr_b,\n    output reg  [DATA_WIDTH-1:0]  dout_b\n);\n    reg [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] memory [0:(2**ADDR_WIDTH)-1];\n    \n    always @(posedge clk) begin\n        if (we_a)\n            memory[addr_a] <= din_a;\n        dout_a <= memory[addr_a];\n        dout_b <= memory[addr_b];\n    end\nendmodule"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Speed \u2190\u2192 Capacity:\n  Registers (fastest, smallest)  \u2192 ~100 bytes\n  L1 Cache (SRAM)               \u2192 32-64 KB\n  L2 Cache (SRAM)               \u2192 256 KB - 1 MB\n  L3 Cache (SRAM)               \u2192 4-32 MB\n  Main Memory (DRAM)            \u2192 4-128 GB\n  Storage (Flash/SSD/HDD)       \u2192 256 GB - TB"
        ]
      ]
    }
